W: 2. Youth must have some dalliance,
W: of good or ill some pastance.
W: Company methinks then best,
W: all thoughts and fancies to digest.
W: For idleness,
W: is chief mistress
W: of vices all
W: Then who can say
W: but mirth and play
W: is best of all.
W:
W: 3. Company with honesty,
W: Is virtue, vices to flee.
W: Company is good and ill,
W: but every man hath his free will.
W: The best ensue,
W: the worst eschew,
W: my mind shall be
W: Virtue to use,
W: vice to refuse,
W: thus shall I use me.
%
